menu "Bootloader policy example"

    config EXAMPLE_CONFIRM_IMAGE
        bool "confirm the image at startup"
        default n
        help
            When disabled, which is the default, the application never confirms itself, so
            every boot is an unconfirmed boot and the policy walks up to the attempt limit
            and then enters safe mode. That is the path the automated test asserts.

            Enable this to see the healthy path: the application records that it started
            successfully, which resets the attempt counter and clears safe mode.

endmenu
